Package: userls
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.11)
Description: read-only CLI to inspect local accounts, groups and sessions
 userls lists the accounts and groups known to the system through NSS
 (pwd and grp, with a getent fallback), classifies each account as normal,
 service, system or unknown using the UID ranges in /etc/login.defs plus
 shell and home-path indicators, and lists the active sessions reported by
 who.
 .
 It is read-only: it never modifies accounts, passwords, groups or system
 files. It needs no root privileges and no network access, and it renders
 aligned tables plus JSON and CSV for scripting.
